Intended change since f22aa8e: a re-key (install on a state that already has a consumer) frees the consumer's layer slot.

f22aa8e replaced the consumer with `g_states[main] = Consumer{...}` and never released a layer slot it held:
g_slot_owner[slot] stayed set, the old layer kept applying, and repeated re-keys used up the 8 slots. The fix is
the same release an uninstall does, in a new install_locked (which the harness's api_ops.inc calls, EQ_BASELINE_FIXED).
Mirrors src/core/lua_api.hpp; see tests/equivalence/README.md, "Intended changes since f22aa8e".

--- a/src/lua_api.hpp
+++ b/src/lua_api.hpp
@@ -628,18 +628,30 @@
     inline constexpr const char* FUNCTION_NAMES[] = {"register", "view",  "live",  "enabled", "layer_set",
                                                      "layer_clear", "layers", "claim", "release", "owner"};
 
+    // Under g_mutex. The bookkeeping of a consumer's (re)start on `main`; returns the mod version to publish.
+    inline auto install_locked(lua_State* main, std::string mod, std::string mod_version) -> std::string
+    {
+        // A Lua mod restarted without an on_lua_stop (a hot reload, a script error at load) comes back on the
+        // same state: whatever it claimed before is not its claim any more, so the camera goes back to nobody,
+        // and the layer slot it held is freed too (its layer fades out), as an uninstall does.
+        if (g_owner_state == main) release_locked(false);
+        if (auto it = g_states.find(main); it != g_states.end() && it->second.slot >= 0)
+        {
+            clear_slot(it->second.slot);
+            g_slot_owner[it->second.slot].clear();
+        }
+        g_mod_version = std::move(mod_version);
+        g_states[main] = Consumer{std::move(mod), false, -1};
+        return g_mod_version;
+    }
+
